  "era_overview": {
    "description": "The LS engine family became the most popular swap engine in history, dominating everything from drag racing to drift cars. GM continued innovation with Gen IV LS engines, then the revolutionary Gen V LT series with direct injection. The flat-plane crank LT6 represents the pinnacle of naturally aspirated V8 development.",
    "key_themes": [
      "LS engine becomes universal swap engine",
      "Gen IV LS adds VVT and AFM",
      "LT direct injection technology",
      "Supercharged LT4/LT5 power",
      "LT6 flat-plane crank masterpiece"
    ]
  },

